===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[methodical|Methodical]] and [[efficient]], in a way that would be [[advantageous]] to a [[business]] or [[businessperson]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1898|author=w:H.G. Wells|title=w:The War of the Worlds|publisher=William Heinemann|location=London|page=|passage=The gunners stood by the guns waiting, and the ammunition waggons were at a '''business-like''' distance.}}
# [[earnest|Earnest]] and [[practical]] without being [[distracted]] or [[enthusiastic]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Rebecca Davis O’Brien|title=Did Ron DeSantis Shake His Wife’s Hand?|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/11/us/politics/desantis-wife-handshake.html|date=11-01-2024|passage=Then, with a '''businesslike''' rigor, he grasped the outstretched palm of Casey DeSantis, Florida’s first lady.}}

